    <item>
      <title>Adam Smith’s Lessons for Investors in the Age of AI</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/news/videos/2026-09-03/adam-smith-s-lessons-for-investors-in-the-age-of-ai-video</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">1614d928d5d9f4b8560ba1cc</guid>
      <pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 08:30:55 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>In this episode of Merryn Talks Money, host Merryn Somerset Webb is joined by Bloomberg Senior Reporter John Stepek, Schroders Head of Strategic Research Duncan Lamont and Nelsons Chairman and Creative Scotland Chair Robert Wilson for a special roundtable recorded at Panmure House during the Edinburgh Fringe Festival. Marking 250 years since the publication of The Wealth of Nations, they ask what Adam Smith can teach the world about artificial intelligence, government intervention and investing.

The panel discusses whether policymakers interfere too much in markets, why holding too much cash can be a risk in itself and whether investors should worry about buying stocks at record highs. They also explore what the rise of AI could mean for jobs, trust and the relationships that hold societies together. (Source: Bloomberg)</description>
